    "claim": "The ndata crate intentionally subverts many of rust's strengths in order to overcome its weaknesses. Don't use a DataArray when a Vec will do, but you should understand the advantages of a DataArray and when using it makes sense -- code boundaries, function signatures, closures, threads. Same goes for HashMap vs DataObject and byte arrays vs DataBytes.",
