    "claim": "The dev app knows NOTHING about the agent library (the owner's rule, 2026-08-10): dev/app carry no agent names, no probes, no availability checks - only generic plugin sockets. One runtime/dev/plugins.json entry (dev.plugins) activates the whole add-on: the boot's union control directory sweeps [own lib, app] plus exactly the plugin_lib values the registry contributes, and dev.session/dev.workbench consume an optional module named `ask` (the ask-provider socket) that the add-on's cluster installs.",
    "detail": "app.store carries no add-on API (agentLibIds/agentLibCall/listTools/chatLlm/describeCommand deleted); the provider owns its own wire via store.invoke - agent.agentloop exports listTools/chatLlm/describeCommand/logTurn/errorHint and agent.ask (module:true, in the agentmodules cluster) re-exports them plus agentprompt's ADDENDUM as the socket adapter. Verified in a real browser (Playwright) on two disposables: a plain instance boots the bench with ZERO agent-library requests and no console errors (notebook stays a REPL, generate button absent); an overlaid instance with the single registry entry gets agent controls in the union directory, the ask module registered, and the notebook wired - no install script involved.",
    "tags": "doctrine,plugins,dev,agent-optional,ask-provider,decoupling",
    "source": {
      "doc": "the owner's directive + browser-verified, session 2026-08-10, branch claude/newbound-missing-library-fixes-bx9bs0 (dev.dev, dev.session, dev.workbench, dev.shelf, dev.chatctx, app.store, agent.agentloop, agent.ask, agent.agentmodules)"
    },
    "confidence": "high",
    "time": 1786366539955
  },
  {
    "claim": "Plugins graft onto things that don't know anything about them (the owner's rule, verbatim, 2026-08-10). A platform surface may expose only GENERIC graft points - a slot element, a small API on that slot, a bubbling DOM event - and must carry zero knowledge of any particular plugin: no names, no probes, no availability checks, no plugin-shaped interfaces. Everything a plugin needs beyond those graft points, the plugin brings itself.",
    "detail": "The reference implementation: dev.session exposes .ss-plugins carrying an nbNotebook API (pushCell/cells/confirmTyped/confirmLite/busy/toast) and an nb-session-open event - agent.askrow grafts the entire chat surface there; dev.workbench renders a .cm-ext slot per command-meta panel and dispatches nb-command-meta - agent.describebtn injects the generate button from a document-level listener; the loader's pluginPass (dev.plugins registry entries with target/selector) is the mount mechanism. Anti-pattern to reject in review: a 'neutral socket' module whose interface mirrors one plugin's export list (the deleted agent.ask) - coupling wearing a neutral badge. Gotcha fixed en route: loader.js pluginEntries read r.status off store.invoke's {envelope,ms} wrapper, so the registry always parsed as empty and the pass had never fired.",
    "tags": "doctrine,plugins,graft,decoupling,dev,notebook,workbench",
    "source": {
      "doc": "the owner's directive + browser-verified on two disposables, session 2026-08-10, branch claude/newbound-missing-library-fixes-bx9bs0 (dev.session, dev.workbench, app.loader, agent.askrow, agent.describebtn; agent.ask deleted)"
    },
    "confidence": "high",
    "time": 1786368120043
  },
  {
    "claim": "One add-on = ONE plugin-registry entry (the owner's refinement, 2026-08-10: if no sane person would ever install just one of the pieces, it's one entry, not three). The single registered payload control brings every other surface itself - static children for what can install at boot, and its own watcher for slots that appear later.",
    "detail": "The reference: the agent add-on registers only agentmodules -> dev.dev. The cluster's children install the shared modules and describebtn (a document-level listener, armed at boot before the workbench exists); the cluster's js watches for the notebook's .ss-plugins slot and installs askrow into it whenever an unclaimed one appears, marking it with the same data-nb-plugin attribute the loader's registry pass uses so the mechanisms coexist. Gotcha: a cluster child installing at boot runs BEFORE the boot publishes __benchPlatform.moduleUrls - resolve shared modules with requireModule(name), the order-free registry, never import(moduleUrls[...]).",
    "tags": "doctrine,plugins,graft,one-entry,cluster,requireModule",
    "source": {
      "doc": "the owner's directive + browser-verified (single-entry disposable), session 2026-08-10, branch claude/newbound-missing-library-fixes-bx9bs0 (agent.agentmodules html+js, agent.askrow, agent.describebtn)"
    },
    "confidence": "high",
    "time": 1786368902316
  },
  {
    "claim": "This is a VERY MATURE platform - versions of it have been around for thirty years - so if you're writing a bunch of scaffolding you probably shouldn't be (the owner, 2026-08-10). Before inventing any mechanism, go find the existing pattern: stock installControl(el, lib, ctl, cb, data), me.ready (fires with your parent's DOM present and your own subtree activated), el.api walking for inter-control APIs, data-control child divs for composition, and the dev.plugins registry for grafts. The platform already solved lifecycle, ordering, and composition.",
    "detail": "The case study: an agent session hand-rolled a MutationObserver, two document-level CustomEvents, and a DOM-property capability protocol (slot.nbNotebook) to graft the ask row and describe button - all of it re-deriving, ambiently and probabilistically, what the stock patterns guarantee lineally. dev.plugins' own js facet is 27 lines and already was the whole pattern: me.ready -> walk up for the host -> read the registry -> installControl at the entry's selector. The collapse replaced everything with: session sets root.api (the stock convention), askrow/describebtn are classic me.ready controls carrying their module deps as hidden data-control child divs (module registration is idempotent - consumers can share deps), and two registry entries mount them. Ambient coupling (document events, page-wide observers, properties stashed on DOM nodes) is also a SECURITY smell: lineal wiring is auditable by reading the parent; ambient wiring requires auditing every script on the page.",
    "tags": "doctrine,scaffolding,mature-platform,stock-patterns,ready,el-api,installControl,security",
    "source": {
      "doc": "the owner's directive, verbatim in the claim, session 2026-08-10, branch claude/newbound-missing-library-fixes-bx9bs0 (dev.session, agent.askrow, agent.describebtn; agent.agentmodules deleted; reference: dev.plugins js facet)"
    },
    "confidence": "high",
    "time": 1786370816243
  },
  {
    "claim": "The knowledge in a graft flows ONE way: the plugin is allowed to know things about what it's grafting onto, not the other way around (the owner, verbatim, 2026-08-10). Corollary: one add-on registers ONE plugins.json entry - a headless entry-point control (target dev.dev, selector \"\": the boot parks it in its hidden holder) that itself knows the host's graft spots and checks them on a heartbeat, filling any unclaimed one.",
    "detail": "The reference: agent.bench is the whole registration - one entry, target dev.dev, selector \"\". Its ready() sets a 250ms setInterval running two querySelectors (.ss-plugins in the notebook drawer, .wb-plugins in the workbench - both lazy-mounted and remounted fresh) and installControls askrow/describebtn into unclaimed spots, stamping the loader pass's own data-nb-plugin marker so the mechanisms coexist. A dumb poll over named spots beats a MutationObserver: same latency in practice, no page-wide mutation surveillance, auditable in five lines. dev carries the spots and nothing else.",
    "tags": "doctrine,plugins,graft,one-entry,knowledge-direction,heartbeat",
    "source": {
      "doc": "the owner's directive + browser-verified (single-entry disposable), session 2026-08-10, branch claude/newbound-missing-library-fixes-bx9bs0 (agent.bench; dev unchanged)"
    },
    "confidence": "high",
    "time": 1786371315474
  },
  {
    "claim": "The platform stands alone (the owner, 2026-08-10): newbound_core and the store libraries carry ZERO knowledge of agent, kb, chat, or LLM - no code, no content, no facet vocabulary, no comments, no UI copy. Verified by unlinking the overlay, regenerating, compiling clean, and grepping the crate empty. kb is data-only (just memories); its write door is agent.archivist.remember; the curriculum is agent.prompts; dev.code is facet-agnostic (any named text facet; only structural record keys refused); the notebook renders command cells and dividers, with custom kinds rendered by whoever registered them (addRenderer); viewctx replaces chatctx.",
    "detail": "Mechanics for future sessions: the MCP deposit tool is agent-archivist-remember now (dev-code-remember is deleted). src/generated_initializer.rs is the ONLY overlay-local file - the committed version is platform-only (no FFI crates); newbound rebuild with the overlay linked regenerates it with agent/kb/scratch and that regeneration stays uncommitted; newbound rebuild ALSO overwrites newbound_core/src/api.rs with overlay sections - git-restore api.rs after an overlay rebuild, commit only the platform-only api.rs. Dylib commands load at startup only via the overlay initializer; one-shot `newbound exec` of a dylib command can race the load. delete_command and delete_control do NOT regenerate mod.rs/api.rs - run rebuild (overlay unlinked) and remove orphaned generated files in the same commit.",
    "tags": "doctrine,separation-of-concerns,platform-standalone,facet-agnostic,kb-data-only,overlay,initializer",
    "source": {
      "doc": "the owner's directives 2026-08-10 + standalone-build verified, branch claude/newbound-missing-library-fixes-bx9bs0 (both repos)"
    },
    "confidence": "high",
    "time": 1786376193672
  },
  {
    "claim": "Vendored ES-module bundles are imported via page-relative URLs (e.g. ../app/asset/app/vendor/nb_three/scenestage.js), never absolute /app/... paths, so tunneled mounts under /peer/remote/UUID/local/ resolve inside the tunnel.",
    "detail": "All newbound URLs are /appname/pagename, so ../ from any page is the (possibly tunneled) instance root — the owner's stated rationale for the relative-URL convention (2026-08-10). The bench layer's origin-rooted URLs (loader ROOT, boot fetches, assetRoots) were tunnel-blind; the collapse removes them. Grep for absolute /app/ in facets as a bug check.",
    "tags": "bench-collapse",
    "confidence": "high",
    "time": 1786399738722
  },
  {
    "claim": "The client platform is api.js alone: controls mount via installControl, shared code lives in LIBRARY controls (idempotent window.NB_* globals defined in ready, dependencies as hidden data-control child divs), and commands are called by name via invokeCommand — there is no module registry, no store layer, no client connection state.",
    "detail": "The owner's collapse, completed 2026-08-10 on branch claude/app-loader-control-oa4cyw. api.js gained one primitive (invokeCommand: lookupID + record read + app/exec over json(), websocket-native and tunnel-relative) and LOST the whole NB_MODULES/requireModule/installModule block. app.nb, app.store, app.loader, app.bridge, app.player, app.modules, dev.devmodules are deleted. ES modules survive only inside vendored bundles (nb_three, nb_codemirror), consumed via browser-native dynamic import of real asset URLs. The saves-ON/writable/mock/connect-dialog posture is gone — server-side security is the gate; session/chat keep the typed-confirm ceremony for non-read-listed commands.",
    "tags": "bench-collapse",
    "confidence": "high",
    "time": 1786403684694
  },
  {
    "claim": "Platform-repo boundary, per the owner (2026-08-11): sessions working on a non-core library make no changes to the newbound repo unless they are genuine bug fixes, and dependencies serving a non-newbound_core library are never added from newbound_core - a library's runtime dependencies are its own packaging concern. Stated while holding back a default.nix change that added ffmpeg/v4l-utils to the platform dev shell for the camera app: the newbound branch claude/camera-app-architecture-owco72 carrying it stays unmerged, and camera's README now brings its own tools into the shell (nix-shell default.nix -p ffmpeg v4l-utils) instead.",
    "tags": "doctrine,newbound,boundary,dependencies,packaging",
    "source": {
      "doc": "the owner's merge instruction, 2026-08-11"
    },
    "confidence": "high",
    "time": 1786471521758
